  "limitations": [
    "One run of one topology, one group mode and one fault class (netem loss 100% on both links of transit r1). It says nothing about partial or one-way loss.",
    "The endpoint routing is a lab workaround: FIPS v0.5.3 does not support two daemons in one namespace, so the lab removes the fd00::/8 route FIPS installs and adds host routes. The result does not show that FIPS supports this.",
    "Each overlay has exactly one route, so FIPS reconvergence is not exercised.",
    "The two overlays share one host, kernel and clock, and four of the six daemons share two namespaces; they are separate fault domains for this fault only.",
    "Each layer is observed at its own resolution (collector per datagram, SRT 500 ms, FIPS about 1 s); temporal ordering does not establish a cause.",
    "The downstream decode runs after the run on the collected stream; it is not a live player."
  ],
